# Shared Packages

Per-package detail: `packages/<pkg>/AGENTS.md`. Shared rules:

- Packages are **leaf-ward**: they may depend on other packages but never on apps.
- Keep public surfaces small and explicit via `exports` in `package.json`. Prefer
  additive changes — removing or renaming an export breaks every consumer.
- `@repo/kafka` — the only place `kafkajs` is used; expose helpers, not clients.
- `@repo/types` — shared contracts; it depends on both `@repo/product-db` and
  `@repo/order-db`, so avoid introducing runtime coupling or cycles. Keep persistence imports type-only.
- `@repo/product-db`, `@repo/inventory-db`, `@repo/user-db`, `@repo/vendor-db` — change `prisma/schema.prisma` and regenerate; never edit
  `generated/**`.
- `@repo/order-db`, `@repo/cart-db` — Mongoose models and connection helpers only.
- `@repo/eslint-config` / `@repo/typescript-config` — shared toolchain configurations.
  Changing these affects all workspaces; verify with `pnpm check-types` and `pnpm lint`.

After changing a package, type-check its dependents too:
`pnpm check-types` from the root.
